  "query_preview": "..\n(Saturday Night through next Friday)\nIssued at 1112 AM CDT Fri Sep 25 2026\n\nTemperatures will be on the rise late this weekend through the\nmiddle of next week as an upper-ridge over the Plains expands\neastward. We'll be back into the 80s and low-90s with low to\nmedium PoPs (20-40%) moving into the region by late \nWednesday/early Thursday. \n\nA closed upper-level low in the southern stream will move eastward\nfrom the Southwest CONUS by midweek. Simultaneously, a northern\nstream shortwave will push from the Rockies and into the Great\nLakes region. The southern stream upper-level low will develop a\nsurface low that will slowly traverse the central CONUS,\neventually dragging a cold front across the area sometime late\nweek. FROPA timing is uncertain at this time, but the pattern\nlooks more unsettled Thursday onward.",
